855858582417,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":63.8,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.11537745027973799,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":71.8,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":1.1561182726089911,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":100.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.02938252432563545,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.06134405709523727,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.07639538584697293,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.03657,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":24.4,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Arrowhead Pharmaceuticals, Inc. develops medicines for the treatment of intractable diseases in the United States. Its pipeline includes Plozasiran to reduce production of apolipoprotein C-III in Phase 3 studies; Zodasiran to reduce production of angiopoietin-like protein 3 in Phase 3 clinical trials; ARO-DIMER-PA, a dual functional RNAi molecule in a Phase 1/2a clinical trials; and ARO-PNPLA3, an investigational RNAi therapeutic in Phase 1 clinical trials. The company also develops ARO-INHBE, to reduce the hepatic expression of the INHBE gene and its secreted gene product, Activin E in Phase 1/2a clinical trials; ARO-ALK7 to silence adipocyte expression of the ACVR1C gene in Phase 1/2a clinical trials; ARO-RAGE to reduce production of the receptor for advanced glycation end products in Phase 1/2a clinical trials; and ARO-MAPT, an investigational RNAi-based therapy. In addition, it is developing ARO-C3 to reduce production of C3 in Phase 1/2a clinical trials; and ARO-CFB to reduce hepatic expression of CFB in a Phase 1/2a clinical trials. The company has collaboration and license Agreements with Glaxosmithkline Intellectual Property (No. 3) Limited; Takeda Pharmaceutical Company Limited; Amgen Inc.; and Sarepta Therapeutics, Inc. Arrowhead Pharmaceuticals, Inc. was founded in 2003 and is headquartered in Pasadena, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Christopher R. Anzalone Ph.D. | Chairman, CEO & President | Age 56 | Compensation: $2.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 711 people. Revenue per employee of $1.2M ranks in the top quartile among Healthcare peers, improving at 76%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $221K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $89K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Arrowhead Pharmaceuticals, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $8.2B market cap on $829M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +51% over the past three years and +116% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +238.0pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -72% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $157M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 19 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -13.1% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 1.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 2.9% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 3.7% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 132% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.3166853680077755},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $14.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 12% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Valued at a 353% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Growing faster than most Healthcare peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Arrowhead Pharmaceuticals (ARWR) Could Be 48% Undervalued Following Its $400 Million Refinancing","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nasdaq-arwr/arrowhead-pharmaceuticals/news/arrowhead-pharmaceuticals-arwr-could-be-48-undervalued-follo","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793928682.485,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.477,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Arrowhead Pharmaceuticals (ARWR) Set to Announce Earnings on Thursday","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/arrowhead-pharmaceuticals-arwr-set-to-announce-earnings-on-thursday.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793873588.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.866,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Does NHS Funding For REDEMPLO Change The Bull Case For Arrowhead Pharmaceuticals (ARWR)?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nasdaq-arwr/arrowhead-pharmaceuticals/news/does-nhs-funding-for-redemplo-change-the-bull-case-for-arrow","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793839726.728,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.361,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How (ARWR) Movements Inform Risk Allocation Models","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/141/How_ARWR_Movements_Inform_Risk_Allocation_Models_103026114601_1793418361.html","date":"2026-10-31","timestamp":1793418361.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"CRISPR Therapeutics (NASDAQ:CRSP) vs. Arrowhead Pharmaceuticals (NASDAQ:ARWR) Head-To-Head Review","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10